      "discover": {
        "kind": "text",
        "title": "Bugünün hava durumu",
        "body": "Good morning! Here's today's weather.\n\nIstanbul: It's cloudy and windy this morning, and it's raining in the afternoon. 14 degrees.\n\nAntalya: It's sunny and hot. Perfect for the beach! 30 degrees.\n\nErzurum: It's very cold. It's snowing in the mountains. Minus 5 degrees.\n\nAnkara: It's sunny but cold. 8 degrees.",
        "questions": [
          {
            "type": "multipleChoice",
            "prompt": "Where is it snowing?",
            "options": [
              "Ankara",
              "Erzurum",
              "Istanbul"
            ],
            "answerIndex": 1,
            "explanation": "\"Erzurum: ... It's snowing in the mountains.\"",
            "id": "a1-u11-l1-d01"
          },
          {
            "type": "multipleChoice",
            "prompt": "What's the weather like in Antalya?",
            "options": [
              "Sunny and hot",
              "Cloudy and windy",
              "Sunny but cold"
            ],
            "answerIndex": 0,
            "explanation": "\"Antalya: It's sunny and hot.\"",
            "id": "a1-u11-l1-d02"
          }
        ]
      },
      "learn": {
        "explanation": "**Hava sormak:** What's the weather like (today / in Antalya)?\n\n**Cevap her zaman It ile başlar:**\n\n- **It's** sunny / cloudy / windy / foggy. (sıfat)\n- **It's** hot / warm / cold. (sıfat)\n- **It's raining.** / **It's snowing.** (şu an oluyor)\n- **It's** twenty degrees. / **It's** minus five.\n\n**Mevsimler:** in spring, in summer, in autumn, in winter\n\n- It **rains** a lot in autumn. (genel)\n- It's **raining** now. (şu an)",
        "examples": [
          {
            "en": "It's sunny but windy.",
            "tr": "Hava güneşli ama rüzgarlı."
          },
          {
            "en": "It's raining in London.",
            "tr": "Londra'da yağmur yağıyor."
          },
          {
            "en": "It's very hot in summer.",
            "tr": "Yazın hava çok sıcak."
          }
        ],
        "turkishNote": "Türkçede özne olmadan \"Yağmur yağıyor\" ya da \"Soğuk\" deriz. İngilizcede cümlenin bir öznesi olmalıdır, bu yüzden It kullanılır: It's cold (Is cold değil). \"Hava\" kelimesini çevirmeye gerek yok: \"The weather is cold\" da doğrudur ama \"It's cold\" çok daha yaygındır."
      },
